1
00:00:00,791 --> 00:00:03,375
I'm glad you've found the path that's right for you.

2
00:00:04,076 --> 00:00:04,845
YOTSAWIT THITICHAROEN
NO. 15 RANKED JUNIOR TENNIS PLAYER

3
00:00:04,845 --> 00:00:07,243
I don't think Sun looks like he did
when he received the trophy in this picture.

4
00:00:07,583 --> 00:00:08,377
Nice shot.

5
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:09,662
But who did it?

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,907
I even let you walk out before me.

7
00:00:14,907 --> 00:00:16,489
You like me that much?

8
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:19,026
Hey, Sun! Wait up!

9
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,419
Have fun waiting for the ferry.

10
00:00:21,419 --> 00:00:22,087
Shit!

11
00:00:22,087 --> 00:00:25,039
What kind of professional steals customers
behind someone's back?

12
00:00:25,039 --> 00:00:26,336
You're the one who started it!

13
00:00:26,336 --> 00:00:27,004
What did I do?

14
00:00:27,004 --> 00:00:29,573
You left a one-star review on
my Google Maps page.

15
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,077
I want us to call a truce.

16
00:00:31,077 --> 00:00:33,050
Because this is my last semester.

17
00:00:34,552 --> 00:00:35,796
You wanna try me?

18
00:00:36,197 --> 00:00:39,578
Well, I hope this tennis club
has something good for me to try.

19
00:00:41,941 --> 00:00:42,716
Here I am.

20
00:00:46,021 --> 00:00:47,966
[2 YEARS AGO]

21
00:00:47,966 --> 00:00:49,259
Why don't you take the ferry?

22
00:00:49,499 --> 00:00:52,329
The new BTS line suits me much better.

23
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:55,130
What's wrong with you two?

24
00:00:55,711 --> 00:00:56,557
What the hell?

25
00:00:56,857 --> 00:00:58,342
It's public transportation.

26
00:00:58,542 --> 00:00:59,851
I'm taking the train.

27
00:01:00,071 --> 00:01:01,645
You take the ferry.

28
00:01:02,226 --> 00:01:05,400
If your dad hadn't picked a fight
with the van driver,

29
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,858
we could've gone home together.

30
00:01:07,218 --> 00:01:08,349
What the hell was the problem?

31
00:01:08,349 --> 00:01:09,684
Why couldn't we just take the van together?

32
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:10,954
Please!

33
00:01:12,977 --> 00:01:14,669
If your dad hadn't started it,

34
00:01:14,669 --> 00:01:15,266
Hey.

35
00:01:15,266 --> 00:01:16,542
Do you think my dad would've said
anything to him?

36
00:01:16,542 --> 00:01:17,398
My dad started it,

37
00:01:17,398 --> 00:01:19,441
but why did your dad have to join in
until the driver got pissed off?

38
00:01:19,441 --> 00:01:21,641
If your dad hadn't started it,
would my dad have joined in?

39
00:01:21,641 --> 00:01:22,798
Hey!

40
00:01:22,898 --> 00:01:24,011
Enough! Look!

41
00:01:24,171 --> 00:01:27,250
You're seriously arguing over
how to get home?

42
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:27,875
-Yes!
-Yes!

43
00:01:29,437 --> 00:01:32,681
His dad yelled at the van driver,
so I had to go home by myself.

44
00:01:32,681 --> 00:01:34,263
-Hey!
-That's not true! His dad started it.

45
00:01:34,263 --> 00:01:36,086
I don’t know about your dads.

46
00:01:40,492 --> 00:01:41,414
Heads or tails?

47
00:01:41,414 --> 00:01:42,145
-Heads!
-Heads!

48
00:01:42,766 --> 00:01:43,534
I called it first.

49
00:01:46,577 --> 00:01:47,329
Hey!

50
00:01:47,669 --> 00:01:48,607
What are you doing?

51
00:01:48,607 --> 00:01:49,433
I've got an idea.

52
00:01:51,221 --> 00:01:52,174
Ready!!

53
00:01:53,636 --> 00:01:54,332
Go!!

54
00:01:55,454 --> 00:01:57,388
Whoever gets there and touches
the statue’s hand first

55
00:01:57,729 --> 00:01:59,086
gets to take the BTS.

56
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:02,556
Deal?

57
00:02:20,257 --> 00:02:21,495
Oh, no.

58
00:02:22,095 --> 00:02:23,229
You missed.

59
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,280
Aren't you an athlete?

60
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,976
I'm heading home first.

61
00:02:31,657 --> 00:02:32,739
Have fun on the ferry.

62
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,544
Bye-bye.

63
00:02:34,884 --> 00:02:35,674
Hey.

64
00:02:36,074 --> 00:02:36,834
Bye-bye.

65
00:02:37,715 --> 00:02:38,398
You...

66
00:02:38,939 --> 00:02:39,724
Sun.

67
00:02:39,884 --> 00:02:40,600
Hey.

68
00:02:41,381 --> 00:02:42,501
Seriously.

69
00:02:43,022 --> 00:02:44,575
Can't you two just go home together?

70
00:02:45,016 --> 00:02:47,304
Or at least wait until Bay leaves
before you head home?

71
00:02:47,425 --> 00:02:48,466
Yeah, exactly.

72
00:02:49,007 --> 00:02:50,920
Why should I be the one waiting?

73
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:55,567
Someone like Bay is just going to
keep messing with me.

74
00:02:56,228 --> 00:02:57,245
If I want this to end,

75
00:02:57,245 --> 00:02:58,961
settling it with a competition
is the right way.

76
00:03:00,603 --> 00:03:03,998
I won't lose next time.

77
00:03:14,052 --> 00:03:16,052
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION,
MINISTRY OF CULTURE

78
00:04:28,825 --> 00:04:32,282
[BAY, JENO, GAWIN, WAN WA
UNDER-15 TENNIS TOURNAMENT
UNDER-19 TENNIS TOURNAMENT]

79
00:04:32,582 --> 00:04:33,287
Okay!

80
00:04:33,988 --> 00:04:34,662
Come on!

81
00:04:35,043 --> 00:04:36,346
This tournament is

82
00:04:36,626 --> 00:04:37,759
single elimination.

83
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,594
The matches are tomorrow,

84
00:04:39,954 --> 00:04:42,879
so go home and get yourselves ready.

85
00:04:42,879 --> 00:04:43,750
See you all tomorrow.

86
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:44,421
Dismissed.

87
00:04:44,421 --> 00:04:45,208
-Yes, Coach.
-Yes.

88
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:48,571
That's too bad.

89
00:04:50,073 --> 00:04:51,642
We're on opposite sides of the bracket.

90
00:04:53,324 --> 00:04:54,721
I wonder if you'll get knocked out
before we even get to face each other.

91
00:04:56,103 --> 00:04:57,534
Keep running your mouth.

92
00:04:58,235 --> 00:04:59,980
If I make it to the finals,

93
00:05:00,841 --> 00:05:01,969
I'd really like to see

94
00:05:02,249 --> 00:05:03,876
if you'll still be talking this big.

95
00:05:04,317 --> 00:05:05,018
Bring it on.

96
00:05:05,018 --> 00:05:05,618
Come on.

97
00:05:05,618 --> 00:05:06,287
You, come on!

98
00:05:06,287 --> 00:05:07,015
Let's go.

99
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:07,708
Let's go.

100
00:05:07,708 --> 00:05:08,697
Let's go. The court's right here.

101
00:05:08,697 --> 00:05:09,376
You two!

102
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,735
The match is tomorrow.

103
00:05:13,436 --> 00:05:14,228
Calm down.

104
00:05:14,709 --> 00:05:16,730
Save your energy, okay?

105
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,431
Shit.

106
00:06:00,603 --> 00:06:02,001
You still know how to play?

107
00:06:06,988 --> 00:06:08,368
Are you serious?

108
00:06:19,323 --> 00:06:20,724
Two custard buns, one pork bun.

109
00:06:22,326 --> 00:06:22,913
Done.

110
00:06:24,595 --> 00:06:25,967
Another order with just one item.

111
00:06:26,948 --> 00:06:29,249
Boat, tell the customer

112
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:32,227
to order through the app next time
if they're only buying one.

113
00:06:32,327 --> 00:06:33,639
It only costs a little more,

114
00:06:33,919 --> 00:06:35,096
and you won't have to deliver it yourself.

115
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:36,670
Okay, Dad.

116
00:06:37,832 --> 00:06:39,080
Here you go, all done.

117
00:06:42,344 --> 00:06:43,716
Hurry up, Boat.

118
00:06:43,876 --> 00:06:44,707
Faster.

119
00:06:45,328 --> 00:06:46,634
Are you a cop or something?

120
00:06:48,597 --> 00:06:49,306
I'm going.

121
00:06:49,306 --> 00:06:50,697
Yeah, good luck.

122
00:06:57,646 --> 00:06:58,843
It's so quiet today.

123
00:07:00,185 --> 00:07:00,854
Bay!

124
00:07:03,097 --> 00:07:04,041
Hey, Dad.

125
00:07:04,261 --> 00:07:05,506
Oh, hey.

126
00:07:06,007 --> 00:07:07,922
What's with all this stuff?

127
00:07:08,282 --> 00:07:09,540
It's for my portfolio.

128
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:10,702
Portfolio?

129
00:07:11,263 --> 00:07:12,926
Right, take care.

130
00:07:12,926 --> 00:07:14,012
-Okay.
-Portfolio.

131
00:07:14,012 --> 00:07:14,958
Hey, Dad!

132
00:07:14,958 --> 00:07:15,458
Huh?

133
00:07:15,458 --> 00:07:17,051
I might be coming home late
for a while.

134
00:07:18,132 --> 00:07:19,172
Coming home late?

135
00:07:20,213 --> 00:07:23,217
Exams are coming up,
so I need to take things seriously.

136
00:07:23,297 --> 00:07:24,050
Seriously?

137
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:25,899
Of course.

138
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,021
Just let me know if you'll
be home late.

139
00:07:28,261 --> 00:07:30,192
That way I won't take any extra orders.

140
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,324
Okay, Dad.

141
00:07:31,324 --> 00:07:31,840
See you later.

142
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,340
Yeah, good luck.

143
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:32,950
-Bye, Dad.
-Yeah, bye.

144
00:07:45,941 --> 00:07:47,510
I'm here, sir.

145
00:07:47,951 --> 00:07:48,961
Coming!

146
00:07:53,888 --> 00:07:54,620
I'm here.

147
00:07:55,722 --> 00:07:56,841
One hundred and forty baht, sir.

148
00:07:56,941 --> 00:07:58,841
Next time you can order through...

149
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:05,800
Kong!

150
00:08:06,441 --> 00:08:07,145
Boat!

151
00:08:08,427 --> 00:08:09,486
Oh, perfect timing.

152
00:08:10,427 --> 00:08:11,313
Give me a ride to school.

153
00:08:11,493 --> 00:08:12,221
What?

154
00:08:12,221 --> 00:08:12,928
Take me to school.

155
00:08:12,928 --> 00:08:13,713
I'm late. Hurry.

156
00:08:14,094 --> 00:08:15,286
Hurry, I'm late. Let's go.

157
00:08:16,248 --> 00:08:16,950
What the...

158
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:17,560
Go!

159
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,623
Get on.

160
00:08:19,284 --> 00:08:20,240
I'm late. Hurry!

161
00:08:28,905 --> 00:08:31,098
Oh, wow.

162
00:08:31,919 --> 00:08:33,341
So you wanted to be close to me, huh?

163
00:08:35,925 --> 00:08:37,024
The other day when I ran into you,

164
00:08:37,164 --> 00:08:38,666
I started craving your shop's siu mai.

165
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:41,277
But I didn't expect you'd deliver it yourself.

166
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:44,909
I don't have class in the morning,
so I help my dad out.

167
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:48,279
Which days don't you have class?

168
00:08:48,559 --> 00:08:49,704
Maybe we can hang out sometime.

169
00:08:51,987 --> 00:08:53,027
I'm not sure.

170
00:08:53,027 --> 00:08:53,691
I can't say yet.

171
00:08:53,691 --> 00:08:54,614
I'll let you know.

172
00:08:56,175 --> 00:08:57,084
Yeah, yeah.

173
00:08:57,605 --> 00:09:00,126
Oh, your brother signed up
for the tryouts too.

174
00:09:00,426 --> 00:09:02,330
If you're free, come cheer him on.

175
00:09:03,432 --> 00:09:04,244
Tryouts for what?

176
00:09:06,327 --> 00:09:07,437
The tennis tryouts.

177
00:09:08,358 --> 00:09:09,212
Bay?

178
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,560
What's your brother's name?

179
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,200
Bay.

180
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:11,985
Yeah.

181
00:09:12,566 --> 00:09:14,087
Why don't you ask him yourself?

182
00:09:23,024 --> 00:09:24,304
Whose racket is this?

183
00:09:25,105 --> 00:09:26,420
It’s mine.

184
00:09:27,281 --> 00:09:28,040
Hey!

185
00:09:28,702 --> 00:09:29,467
What the...

186
00:09:30,809 --> 00:09:31,837
Careful!

187
00:09:32,097 --> 00:09:33,256
This racket's pretty old.

188
00:09:38,083 --> 00:09:39,397
You used to play tennis?

189
00:09:40,158 --> 00:09:40,881
I did.

190
00:09:41,482 --> 00:09:42,694
But that was over ten years ago.

191
00:09:43,295 --> 00:09:45,630
Damn, that's cool.

192
00:09:45,630 --> 00:09:46,521
Of course.

193
00:09:46,841 --> 00:09:48,223
How good were you?

194
00:09:48,223 --> 00:09:49,575
Are you gonna wipe the floor with Sun?

195
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,200
You're comparing me to him?

196
00:09:55,681 --> 00:09:56,784
"Wipe the floor," my ass.

197
00:09:56,784 --> 00:09:58,053
He's making the national team.

198
00:09:59,074 --> 00:10:00,404
Then why'd you sign up?

199
00:10:00,925 --> 00:10:03,442
Feeling nostalgic about your
tennis days?

200
00:10:05,565 --> 00:10:06,298
Yeah.

201
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:08,482
I just wanted to play tennis again.

202
00:10:12,728 --> 00:10:13,894
You don't believe me?

203
00:10:14,394 --> 00:10:15,093
I do...

204
00:10:15,654 --> 00:10:17,320
not believe you one bit.

205
00:10:18,221 --> 00:10:19,048
Asshole.

206
00:10:19,048 --> 00:10:21,239
Since he's leaving,

207
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:22,613
before he goes,

208
00:10:22,613 --> 00:10:24,570
I want to mess with him one last time.

209
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:25,770
I don't care if I lose.

210
00:10:26,010 --> 00:10:28,271
At least I'll get to annoy him for a day or two.

211
00:10:35,661 --> 00:10:37,822
The teacher sent me to
pick up the forms.

212
00:10:39,384 --> 00:10:40,422
You're so diligent.

213
00:10:40,742 --> 00:10:41,916
Picking them up during lunch break.

214
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,175
Oh, I forgot.

215
00:10:46,175 --> 00:10:48,246
You were asleep when everyone else
turned theirs in.

216
00:10:48,847 --> 00:10:50,405
Why didn't you tell me?

217
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:51,181
Shit.

218
00:10:52,563 --> 00:10:53,127
Hold on.

219
00:11:00,339 --> 00:11:00,935
Here.

220
00:11:06,618 --> 00:11:07,483
Have you tighten your strings?

221
00:11:10,187 --> 00:11:10,952
Why?

222
00:11:11,673 --> 00:11:12,777
If I haven't,

223
00:11:13,218 --> 00:11:14,675
you want to tighten my strings?

224
00:11:15,797 --> 00:11:17,312
I know you always have an excuse ready.

225
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:20,203
I just don't want you blaming broken strings,
that's all.

226
00:11:20,604 --> 00:11:22,079
Yeah, yeah.

227
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:23,347
I've already done it.

228
00:11:23,607 --> 00:11:24,840
Thanks for your concern.

229
00:11:27,704 --> 00:11:30,648
"I don't want you to have an excuse."

230
00:11:31,089 --> 00:11:32,673
He won't even be here next semester.

231
00:11:33,013 --> 00:11:35,119
Can't you just let him be happy
for a little while?

232
00:11:38,183 --> 00:11:39,481
Why do you hate him so much?

233
00:11:53,616 --> 00:11:54,608
Honestly...

234
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:56,685
I...

235
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:00,732
Hey!

236
00:12:01,233 --> 00:12:02,122
Did you get the form?

237
00:12:04,185 --> 00:12:04,855
Yeah.

238
00:12:09,912 --> 00:12:11,355
I don't really hate him.

239
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,920
[Tryouts]

240
00:12:58,519 --> 00:12:59,621
Hey, hey, hey!

241
00:13:00,324 --> 00:13:01,596
What now, Chun?

242
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,413
Here to steal my supplier again?

243
00:13:05,386 --> 00:13:08,580
I came to ask
if you're plotting something again.

244
00:13:08,995 --> 00:13:11,255
Why did your son sign up
for the tryouts?

245
00:13:11,453 --> 00:13:12,534
What the hell are you talking about?

246
00:13:12,858 --> 00:13:16,477
I heard your son entered the competition
that Sun gave up his spot in.

247
00:13:18,135 --> 00:13:20,438
Bay's playing tennis again?

248
00:13:20,907 --> 00:13:22,673
Oh, my.

249
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:25,564
What kind of father are you, huh?

250
00:13:25,943 --> 00:13:28,704
You don't even know what your own
son is up to, Bee?

251
00:13:28,704 --> 00:13:29,362
Huh?

252
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:32,127
But that's okay.

253
00:13:32,722 --> 00:13:38,148
Sun was worried Bay wouldn’t have
enough time to prepare for university,

254
00:13:38,148 --> 00:13:42,091
so he entered the competition just to
eliminate him.

255
00:13:44,218 --> 00:13:44,937
Oh.

256
00:13:44,937 --> 00:13:45,817
Confused?

257
00:13:47,439 --> 00:13:48,111
Bye.

258
00:13:49,192 --> 00:13:49,946
You asshole!

259
00:13:50,631 --> 00:13:51,401
That's all?

260
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:53,859
You smartass!

261
00:13:57,442 --> 00:13:59,259
Bay! Bay!

262
00:14:01,548 --> 00:14:03,949
[SUN]
Bay.

263
00:14:05,715 --> 00:14:06,301
Boat!

264
00:14:07,473 --> 00:14:08,093
Boat!!

265
00:14:09,535 --> 00:14:10,552
Yes, Dad.

266
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,978
Get over here, quick.

267
00:14:11,978 --> 00:14:12,589
Boat.

268
00:14:12,949 --> 00:14:13,753
What is it, Dad?

269
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:16,697
Did you know about this?

270
00:14:22,032 --> 00:14:23,472
I only found out this morning.

271
00:14:24,031 --> 00:14:25,451
This morning?

272
00:14:32,537 --> 00:14:34,101
[SUN]

273
00:14:48,161 --> 00:14:48,849
How was that?

274
00:14:49,228 --> 00:14:49,982
So exhausting.

275
00:14:50,270 --> 00:14:51,126
Me too.

276
00:14:51,757 --> 00:14:52,446
Good job.

277
00:14:52,446 --> 00:14:53,397
See you later.

278
00:14:53,397 --> 00:14:54,170
Yes. Thank you.

279
00:14:54,170 --> 00:14:55,364
Yay!

280
00:15:00,148 --> 00:15:02,069
[JENO, BAY]

281
00:15:04,993 --> 00:15:05,877
How's it going?

282
00:15:06,544 --> 00:15:07,302
They're in the third set.

283
00:15:07,302 --> 00:15:08,726
They split the first two sets.

284
00:15:09,645 --> 00:15:11,306
Bay got crushed in the first set,

285
00:15:11,306 --> 00:15:12,508
both on serve and return.

286
00:15:12,508 --> 00:15:14,786
But in the second set,
they had a lot of long rallies.

287
00:15:14,786 --> 00:15:16,062
In the end, Bay managed to win it.

288
00:15:16,747 --> 00:15:18,013
It'll be over in the next game.

289
00:15:18,211 --> 00:15:19,562
Just watch how he plays.

290
00:15:19,562 --> 00:15:20,898
Bay never lets up.

291
00:15:21,204 --> 00:15:22,705
That's how power players are.

292
00:15:22,957 --> 00:15:25,806
Even if his opponent is great at
placing shots,

293
00:15:26,022 --> 00:15:27,508
once the rallies drag on,
they lose focus.

294
00:15:28,607 --> 00:15:30,183
When Bay works on his art,

295
00:15:30,435 --> 00:15:31,841
he has to stay focused on one thing
for a long time.

296
00:15:33,481 --> 00:15:34,782
That's why he has good concentration.

297
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,735
Are you complimenting him?

298
00:15:39,537 --> 00:15:40,167
No.

299
00:15:40,888 --> 00:15:41,830
I'm not complimenting him.

300
00:15:42,605 --> 00:15:43,727
I'm just saying what I see.

301
00:15:45,081 --> 00:15:46,798
Besides, his skills are...

302
00:15:47,627 --> 00:15:48,373
so-so.

303
00:15:49,058 --> 00:15:50,137
They're nowhere near mine.

304
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:52,858
Wow.

305
00:15:57,497 --> 00:15:58,806
I'm gonna get going, okay?

306
00:15:59,076 --> 00:16:00,830
-Yeah, see you.
-See you.

307
00:16:00,938 --> 00:16:01,621
Bye.

308
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:02,994
Coach.

309
00:16:03,409 --> 00:16:04,260
I'm leaving.

310
00:16:25,398 --> 00:16:26,174
Hey, bro.

311
00:16:26,931 --> 00:16:27,580
Oh, hey.

312
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:28,354
Over here.

313
00:16:29,670 --> 00:16:31,055
Well, well.

314
00:16:31,055 --> 00:16:33,083
I thought all you did was chase
after clients.

315
00:16:33,083 --> 00:16:35,228
Didn't think you'd have time
to see your little brother.

316
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,703
The last time I stood you up,

317
00:16:39,009 --> 00:16:40,836
I really had to meet an important client.

318
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,392
Sorry.

319
00:16:44,852 --> 00:16:45,702
By the way...

320
00:16:46,225 --> 00:16:50,728
are there any teachers at your school
interested in buying insurance?

321
00:16:50,728 --> 00:16:52,773
Oh, God. Stop it.

322
00:16:52,773 --> 00:16:54,871
We haven't seen each other in forever,
and you're still the same.

323
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:59,544
By the way, how's Mom?

324
00:17:01,959 --> 00:17:02,856
She's doing great.

325
00:17:03,919 --> 00:17:05,736
I think she's gotten used to
living like this.

326
00:17:07,556 --> 00:17:08,209
Hey.

327
00:17:08,606 --> 00:17:10,385
You don't need to get involved
in grown-ups' problems.

328
00:17:10,926 --> 00:17:11,733
Anyway...

329
00:17:12,003 --> 00:17:12,995
when are you leaving?

330
00:17:13,986 --> 00:17:14,652
Huh?

331
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:16,935
Leaving where?

332
00:17:17,025 --> 00:17:19,249
For your training camp,
or whatever it's called.

333
00:17:20,222 --> 00:17:21,662
Oh.

334
00:17:22,473 --> 00:17:24,086
Hey, you're still young.
You're already getting forgetful?

335
00:17:25,276 --> 00:17:26,536
I didn't forget.

336
00:17:26,987 --> 00:17:27,848
It's just...

337
00:17:28,713 --> 00:17:30,130
things have been a little hectic lately.

338
00:17:30,490 --> 00:17:31,020
Why?

339
00:17:31,417 --> 00:17:32,701
Are you having problems at school?

340
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:35,191
No, it's just...

341
00:17:35,533 --> 00:17:36,262
You'd better not.

342
00:17:37,542 --> 00:17:38,134
By the way...

343
00:17:39,107 --> 00:17:42,082
come by the house sometime.

344
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:44,921
So Papa can yell at me?

345
00:17:45,318 --> 00:17:47,153
Papa doesn't yell anymore.

346
00:17:48,829 --> 00:17:49,509
Bro,

347
00:17:50,284 --> 00:17:51,367
don't overthink it.

348
00:17:51,854 --> 00:17:52,515
Okay?

349
00:17:56,174 --> 00:17:56,933
Yeah, maybe later.

350
00:17:57,059 --> 00:17:58,069
Now's not the right time.

351
00:18:00,033 --> 00:18:01,205
Hey,
is there anything you want to eat?

352
00:18:01,908 --> 00:18:03,727
We hardly ever get to see each other.
Whatever you want, it's on me.

353
00:18:06,287 --> 00:18:07,273
That place.

354
00:18:07,868 --> 00:18:08,488
That one.

355
00:18:08,488 --> 00:18:09,505
I want to eat there.

356
00:18:27,055 --> 00:18:27,742
Hey, bro.

357
00:18:28,859 --> 00:18:29,797
- Yeah?
- Can I ask you something?

358
00:18:30,914 --> 00:18:32,300
Do you know this loser?

359
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,336
You go to the same school, right?

360
00:18:35,354 --> 00:18:36,862
He doesn't look familiar.

361
00:18:37,349 --> 00:18:40,257
I don't really have many friends
at school.

362
00:18:41,050 --> 00:18:43,120
I don't really hang out with anyone.

363
00:18:43,607 --> 00:18:44,465
Thanks, anyway.

364
00:18:44,465 --> 00:18:45,313
You're welcome.

365
00:19:30,404 --> 00:19:31,180
Oh.

366
00:19:32,730 --> 00:19:33,386
You're home late.

367
00:19:34,936 --> 00:19:36,599
I was working on a project, Dad.

368
00:19:37,356 --> 00:19:38,618
Let me see it.

369
00:19:38,816 --> 00:19:39,617
What kind of project are you working on?

370
00:19:40,356 --> 00:19:41,384
It's not finished yet, Dad.

371
00:19:41,961 --> 00:19:43,246
You wouldn't understand it
if you looked at it now.

372
00:19:43,788 --> 00:19:45,304
I'll understand.

373
00:19:45,754 --> 00:19:49,267
I want to know what my youngest son
has been working on.

374
00:19:50,421 --> 00:19:52,047
That might not be a good idea, Dad.

375
00:19:52,444 --> 00:19:53,372
It's late.

376
00:19:53,372 --> 00:19:54,623
I'm just going to bed.

377
00:19:54,731 --> 00:19:56,632
What's in your bag?

378
00:19:56,993 --> 00:19:58,037
Let me see.

379
00:19:58,325 --> 00:19:59,322
Do you really have to?

380
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,577
Let me see.

381
00:20:22,799 --> 00:20:24,441
How did the tryouts go today?

382
00:20:26,766 --> 00:20:28,043
I almost lost, Dad.

383
00:20:29,863 --> 00:20:31,721
But I pulled through in the end.

384
00:20:38,534 --> 00:20:39,499
What about Sun?

385
00:20:40,995 --> 00:20:42,496
He won by a landslide.

386
00:20:42,802 --> 00:20:44,393
He finished in the very first match.

387
00:20:49,766 --> 00:20:50,855
Take it easy, Dad.

388
00:20:51,396 --> 00:20:53,051
But if you're really not okay with this,

389
00:20:54,241 --> 00:20:55,696
I'll withdraw.

390
00:20:57,463 --> 00:20:58,771
I'll just say I hurt my shoulder,

391
00:21:00,393 --> 00:21:03,614
so you won't have to lose face to Sun.

392
00:21:03,866 --> 00:21:05,164
Come on, honey.

393
00:21:05,452 --> 00:21:07,251
If he wants to play, just let him play.

394
00:21:07,521 --> 00:21:09,484
Even if he loses, it's no big deal.

395
00:21:10,944 --> 00:21:11,634
Bay!!

396
00:21:15,383 --> 00:21:16,651
You have to keep competing.

397
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,589
Keep going.

398
00:21:20,114 --> 00:21:21,801
You won today even though

399
00:21:21,801 --> 00:21:23,881
you haven't touched a tennis racket
in ten years.

400
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:28,990
That means you've got real talent.

401
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:30,760
Real talent.

402
00:21:30,850 --> 00:21:32,054
If you win, great.

403
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:33,837
That family will finally lose face too.

404
00:21:34,774 --> 00:21:36,709
But he's a professional athlete, Dad.

405
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,206
So what if he is?

406
00:21:39,422 --> 00:21:40,694
If we lose, all we lose is face.

407
00:21:40,694 --> 00:21:44,945
But if we win,
we've got everything to gain.

408
00:21:45,414 --> 00:21:46,092
Right?

409
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,089
Here's the deal.

410
00:21:49,152 --> 00:21:51,887
If you beat Sun,

411
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,713
whatever you want,

412
00:21:54,045 --> 00:21:54,859
I'll give it to you.

413
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,575
You promise?

414
00:21:58,575 --> 00:22:00,014
You have my word.

415
00:22:00,014 --> 00:22:00,984
-Just wait and see.
-Go for it.

416
00:22:00,984 --> 00:22:02,430
Oh, honey!

417
00:22:02,430 --> 00:22:03,855
I have to get up early to practice!

418
00:22:05,166 --> 00:22:06,703
Oh, your net game...

419
00:22:06,811 --> 00:22:08,657
Like father, like son.

420
00:22:08,657 --> 00:22:09,943
Wake me up at five-thirty
tomorrow, Dad.

421
00:22:19,598 --> 00:22:22,227
SUN

422
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:26,365
Oh, Sun.

423
00:22:26,598 --> 00:22:28,321
You dragged the match out so long today
the junior was completely exhausted.

424
00:22:28,321 --> 00:22:29,865
You should've gone a little easier on him.

425
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,727
Oh, how'd it go?
Did you get the result?

426
00:22:34,233 --> 00:22:34,984
Yep.

427
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,682
SUN VS. BAY

428
00:22:49,063 --> 00:22:50,875
Damn.

429
00:22:51,283 --> 00:22:52,085
Yes!!

430
00:22:53,679 --> 00:22:55,640
Tomorrow's going to be fun.

431
00:22:56,788 --> 00:22:58,173
It's gonna be intense, P'Sun.

432
00:23:11,719 --> 00:23:12,375
Oh, well.

433
00:23:13,269 --> 00:23:14,572
You've been waiting for me?

434
00:23:18,968 --> 00:23:20,351
Can't I get home in peace for once?

435
00:23:23,743 --> 00:23:24,934
Am gonna catch the ferry today?

436
00:23:25,831 --> 00:23:27,266
What's going on with that school?

437
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,455
What school? It's nothing.

438
00:23:28,455 --> 00:23:30,150
Oh, please. Don't even.

439
00:23:30,578 --> 00:23:31,436
How'd you find out about that?

440
00:23:31,514 --> 00:23:33,062
So? Just tell me.

441
00:23:34,210 --> 00:23:34,965
What?

442
00:23:35,451 --> 00:23:36,498
Just tell me.

443
00:23:46,233 --> 00:23:47,501
When are we gonna get home?

444
00:23:47,501 --> 00:23:48,269
We're here.

445
00:23:48,444 --> 00:23:49,406
Boy Hey, Zippo!

446
00:23:49,503 --> 00:23:50,850
You worm face!

447
00:23:52,114 --> 00:23:52,863
Umm...

448
00:23:53,213 --> 00:23:54,277
Who are you guys?

449
00:23:54,549 --> 00:23:55,609
Do I know you?

450
00:23:55,784 --> 00:23:58,277
Boy Did you make Minami-chan cry?

451
00:23:59,425 --> 00:23:59,985
Umm...

452
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,071
I think...

453
00:24:01,674 --> 00:24:03,772
there must be a misunderstanding.

454
00:24:03,772 --> 00:24:06,396
Just let him talk to Minami himself, okay?

455
00:24:06,396 --> 00:24:07,194
Boy Too late for that.

456
00:24:07,194 --> 00:24:09,204
I'm here to get revenge for my sister.

457
00:24:09,924 --> 00:24:11,057
Get them!

458
00:24:20,918 --> 00:24:21,883
Son of a bitch!

459
00:24:24,003 --> 00:24:24,503
Let's go.

460
00:24:31,405 --> 00:24:32,147
Hey.

461
00:24:32,944 --> 00:24:33,926
You okay?

462
00:24:38,477 --> 00:24:39,772
Why wouldn't I be?

463
00:24:43,117 --> 00:24:44,151
Wow.

464
00:24:44,676 --> 00:24:47,540
I just saved you, and you can't
even say thanks.

465
00:24:52,927 --> 00:24:53,917
Shit!

466
00:24:55,065 --> 00:24:55,803
Ow!

467
00:24:58,079 --> 00:24:59,922
That freaking hurts.

468
00:25:02,683 --> 00:25:03,315
Sun!

469
00:25:07,711 --> 00:25:08,891
Did Bay make it to the next round?

470
00:25:15,173 --> 00:25:17,505
Sun, listen to Papa.

471
00:25:18,186 --> 00:25:19,969
Don't underestimate him.

472
00:25:20,319 --> 00:25:20,832
You hear me?

473
00:25:20,832 --> 00:25:21,725
That family...

474
00:25:21,725 --> 00:25:25,614
if they get the chance, they'll suck us dry.

475
00:25:26,139 --> 00:25:28,240
Do you understand that pain?

476
00:25:31,060 --> 00:25:31,858
Yes, Papa.

477
00:25:32,675 --> 00:25:35,168
So don't just beat them.

478
00:25:35,810 --> 00:25:36,551
Crush them.

479
00:25:36,551 --> 00:25:38,840
Don't leave them any chance to come back.

480
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:39,530
Understand?

481
00:25:41,786 --> 00:25:43,121
Get plenty of rest tonight.

482
00:25:43,121 --> 00:25:43,714
Got it?

483
00:25:54,121 --> 00:25:56,372
PORTFOLIO
BENYU THARNWEERANAN

484
00:26:01,137 --> 00:26:01,878
Hey.

485
00:26:02,773 --> 00:26:04,240
When did you find the time to finish it?

486
00:26:04,940 --> 00:26:05,780
Last night.

487
00:26:06,091 --> 00:26:07,030
Why'd you rush it?

488
00:26:07,516 --> 00:26:09,119
You had until tonight, didn't you?

489
00:26:09,333 --> 00:26:10,461
I'm busy today.

490
00:26:10,811 --> 00:26:11,969
I've got a match this evening.

491
00:26:12,961 --> 00:26:13,631
You coming?

492
00:26:14,175 --> 00:26:14,789
Huh?

493
00:26:17,785 --> 00:26:19,083
PORTFOLIO
BENYU THARNWEERANAN

494
00:26:19,083 --> 00:26:20,509
Aren't you focusing on the wrong thing?

495
00:26:22,321 --> 00:26:24,555
At first you said you just wanted
to mess with Sun.

496
00:26:25,527 --> 00:26:27,789
But this portfolio is your future, isn't it?

497
00:26:28,742 --> 00:26:30,242
This match is my future too.

498
00:26:31,117 --> 00:26:32,453
Hey, don't forget.

499
00:26:32,842 --> 00:26:34,206
He's a professional athlete.

500
00:26:35,178 --> 00:26:36,021
So what?

501
00:26:36,585 --> 00:26:37,753
If I believe I can do it,

502
00:26:37,753 --> 00:26:39,104
then I can do it.

503
00:26:39,357 --> 00:26:40,185
Just watch.

504
00:26:40,399 --> 00:26:41,693
I'm going to beat Sun.

505
00:26:43,696 --> 00:26:44,814
Don't forget to come watch.

506
00:26:47,090 --> 00:26:48,296
Damn.

507
00:26:49,268 --> 00:26:50,744
You're not messing around.

508
00:26:56,912 --> 00:26:57,763
Ow!

509
00:26:58,444 --> 00:26:59,812
Are you sure you're okay?

510
00:27:00,084 --> 00:27:01,292
Shouldn't you postpone the match?

511
00:27:04,054 --> 00:27:04,775
I'm fine.

512
00:27:05,572 --> 00:27:06,914
I didn't pull a muscle.

513
00:27:08,509 --> 00:27:09,203
It's just...

514
00:27:09,631 --> 00:27:11,159
a little bruised
where I got kicked.

515
00:27:11,757 --> 00:27:13,676
I only put these on just in case.

516
00:27:14,901 --> 00:27:16,111
I'm really sorry.

517
00:27:17,239 --> 00:27:20,233
Hey, it's okay.
Don't worry about it.

518
00:27:20,544 --> 00:27:21,882
I told you, I'm not hurt that badly.

519
00:27:22,563 --> 00:27:23,405
You don't have to blame yourself.

520
00:27:24,008 --> 00:27:24,750
See?

521
00:27:24,750 --> 00:27:25,865
I can still rotate my arm.

522
00:27:25,865 --> 00:27:27,768
Hey! Don't push it.

523
00:27:27,768 --> 00:27:28,465
See?

524
00:27:29,185 --> 00:27:30,620
I told you I'm fine.

525
00:27:31,262 --> 00:27:32,252
Don't worry about me.

526
00:27:33,730 --> 00:27:34,453
Okay?

527
00:27:47,196 --> 00:27:48,028
What did Sun say?

528
00:27:49,389 --> 00:27:50,700
He refused to postpone the match.

529
00:27:50,841 --> 00:27:51,805
Then neither will I.

530
00:27:52,486 --> 00:27:53,832
And I'm not going easy on him either.

531
00:27:55,291 --> 00:27:57,009
But this is all my fault.

532
00:27:57,121 --> 00:27:59,861
If I don't compete, that means
I'm disrespecting Sun.

533
00:28:00,055 --> 00:28:00,707
Right?

534
00:28:13,788 --> 00:28:14,307
Boat!

535
00:28:17,205 --> 00:28:18,104
Hi, Kong.

536
00:28:19,401 --> 00:28:20,966
You here to cheer on your brother?

537
00:28:21,588 --> 00:28:22,321
Yeah.

538
00:28:26,094 --> 00:28:27,191
Did Dad make you come?

539
00:28:27,385 --> 00:28:28,502
You know it.

540
00:28:29,261 --> 00:28:31,310
And you know,
if you win, we're having a celebration.

541
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:31,810
Oh.

542
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:33,235
But if you lose,

543
00:28:35,005 --> 00:28:36,122
you're in big trouble.

544
00:28:36,803 --> 00:28:38,556
That sends chills down my spine.

545
00:28:39,879 --> 00:28:40,622
-Come on.
-Go!

546
00:28:40,622 --> 00:28:41,457
Is the player ready?

547
00:28:41,651 --> 00:28:42,297
Ready!

548
00:28:42,511 --> 00:28:43,552
What about you?

549
00:28:43,902 --> 00:28:44,453
Ready!

550
00:28:44,453 --> 00:28:45,184
Okay.

551
00:28:45,184 --> 00:28:46,512
If you're ready,
come to the center of the court.

552
00:28:46,512 --> 00:28:47,146
Let's go.

553
00:28:48,449 --> 00:28:49,519
Bay!

554
00:28:50,161 --> 00:28:51,186
You got this!

555
00:28:51,361 --> 00:28:52,377
Thanks, man.

556
00:28:53,081 --> 00:28:54,721
We'll toss a coin
to decide first serve.

557
00:28:55,265 --> 00:28:56,131
You call it first.

558
00:28:56,792 --> 00:28:57,498
Heads.

559
00:28:57,926 --> 00:28:58,784
And you?

560
00:28:58,784 --> 00:28:59,639
Tails.

561
00:28:59,639 --> 00:29:00,352
Okay.

562
00:29:03,911 --> 00:29:04,669
You serve first.

563
00:29:46,046 --> 00:29:46,889
SUN, BAY

564
00:29:53,463 --> 00:29:54,689
SET 1: SUN 2, BAY 0

565
00:29:55,175 --> 00:29:56,796
SUN 3, BAY 0

566
